AccountV3SecurityModule
├── given a canonical linked library and an authenticated real proxy
│   ├── it should bind the library address and captured runtime hash to implementation code
│   ├── full production Account should retain the 20k budget; test-only observation views stay below EIP-170
│   ├── canonical policy reads should use the pinned library and preserve the signed format
│   ├── public fixed-size snapshots should match account state without writes or emitted events
│   ├── an implementation snapshot should never invent an initialized account identity
│   ├── proposals, freeze and nonces remain visible until an explicit transition
│   ├── when two accounts share the library
│   │   └── it should keep authority, counters, storage and event emitters account-local
│   └── when signatures target the library's EIP-712 domain
│       └── it should reject them and accept signatures for the proxy domain
├── given a direct CALL to any state-changing library entrypoint
│   └── it should reject it before reading or writing the library namespace
├── given the internal initial-policy installer selector
│   └── it should not be callable through the account's public dispatch
├── given absent library code at implementation construction
│   └── it should reject deployment
├── given a factory constructed after library drift or with another link target
│   └── it should reject inconsistent composition instead of capturing it as valid
└── given missing or corrupted code after implementation construction
    ├── it should reject every typed entrypoint before delegation or mutation
    └── it should retain state for fuzzed runtime code and entrypoints
